\name{cellucid_expression_transform_set}
\alias{cellucid_expression_transform_set}
\title{Set the expression values}
\usage{
cellucid_expression_transform_set(viewer, log1p, normalize)
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
\item{log1p}{ln(1 + x), after the normalization when both are on. \code{TRUE} or \code{FALSE}. Left out unless given (the viewer then chooses as its own control does).}
\item{normalize}{Each cell's values scaled to 10,000 counts: x \ifelse{latex}{<U+00B7>}{·} 10,000 / the cell's total. \code{TRUE} or \code{FALSE}. Left out unless given (the viewer then chooses as its own control does).}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns its outcome (what it did, as names, counts and ids), or \code{NULL} when it had nothing to report; \code{request$step} is the history step it made.
}
\description{
Show and analyze the genes normalized to 10,000 counts per cell and/or log1p (Data mapping \ifelse{latex}{<U+203A>}{›} Expression values; scanpy normalize_total(target_sum=1e4) then log1p). One setting for coloring, legends, filters, the cell card, reads and every analysis (pseudobulk differential expression always sums raw counts). The person's setting: an agent changes it only when the person asks. Offered when the mapped matrix holds counts; normalizing reads each cell's total from an obs column, else sums every gene once (heavy on a large matrix: asked first).
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{expression.transform.set} (Data). It changes the viewer's state: one step of the viewer's history, labeled as R's, undone like any other. The state it can change: \code{expression}, \code{filters}, \code{colors}.
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{cellucid_act}()} sends any action by its type, and \code{\link{cellucid_action_result}()}
collects its answer.
}
\examples{
if (interactive() && requireNamespace("SeuratObject", quietly = TRUE)) {
  data("pbmc_small", package = "SeuratObject")
  viewer <- cellucid_view(SeuratObject::UpdateSeuratObject(pbmc_small))
  request <- cellucid_expression_transform_set(viewer)
  print(request)
  # cellucid_action_result(request) waits for its outcome.
  cellucid_stop(viewer)
}
}
